    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for that. I'm a bit worried about the \"omitting the field\" part though. In our local database, if a field is empty, it can sometimes cause issues with the indexing or how the items appear in the discovery layer. \n\nIs there a way to use a controlled vocabulary or some kind of standardized placeholder that indicates the creator is definitely unidentifiable, rather than just missing by mistake? I want to make sure a researcher doesn't think the data is just incomplete due to a cataloging error.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
